<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9149" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνοιδ-έω</span></b> , 
			Ep.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνοιδ-είω</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			Nic.
			<u>Th.</u>
			855
		</span></i>: fut.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ήσω</span>: aor.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνῴδησα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hipp.</u>
					1210
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ti.</u>
				84e
			</span></i>: pf.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνῴδηκα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Acut.</u>
					10
				</span></i>
			:—<i>swell up,</i> Hp.l.c.; of a wave, E.l.c., cf.
				<i><span class="en">
				Alciphr.
				1.10
			</span></i>; of wind in the body, Pl.l.c.; of figs ripening, Nic.l.c.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ στέρνα ἀνῴδει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aeschin.
					<u>Ep.</u>
					1.2
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ κάλυμμα ἀνῳδηκός</span>”
				<i>swollen out, inflated,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>HA</u>
					625a2
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>GA</u>
				728b28
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θυμὸς ἀνοιδέει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					7.39
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀργαῖς . . -ούσαις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phld.
					<u>Ir.</u>
					p.63
				</span></i>
			 W.; of anger, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνοιδήσας ὁ βασιλεύς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philostr.
					<u>VA</u>
					7.33
				</span></i>
			 (so in 
				Med.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θυμὸν ἀνοιδήσαντο</span>
			they <i>swelled</i> with rage, <i><span class="en">
				Q.S.
				9.345
			</span></i>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνοιδούσης τῆς νόσου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philostr.
					<u>VA</u>
					4.4
				</span></i>
			.</div>
